---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
import { fullDate } from '../lib/format';

// Keep these in sync with supabase/migrations/*_automation.sql and the provider setup.
const RETENTION_MESSAGES = '12 months';
const RETENTION_RATE_LIMIT = '24 hours';
const DATABASE_REGION = 'Sydney, Australia';
const updated = fullDate(`${SITE.privacyVersion}T12:00:00+13:00`);
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy notice" description="How carlos.nz handles personal information, under the New Zealand Privacy Act 2020.">
  <section class="container-site pb-24 pt-12 md:pt-16">
    <SectionHeading
      level="h1"
      icon="material-symbols:shield-outline"
      kicker="Privacy"
      title="Privacy notice"
      intro={`Plain-language summary first, details below. Version ${SITE.privacyVersion}, last updated ${updated}.`}
    />

    <div class="card mt-10 max-w-3xl p-6 md:p-8">
      <h2 class="text-h3 font-bold">The short version</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-muted marker:text-accent">
        <li>This site has <strong class="text-fg">no analytics, no advertising and no tracking cookies</strong>.</li>
        <li>The only personal information I collect is what you type into the <a class="text-accent underline" href="/contact/">contact form</a>, and I use it only to reply to you.</li>
        <li>Messages are deleted automatically after {RETENTION_MESSAGES}. You can ask me to delete yours sooner, see it, or correct it at any time.</li>
        <li>I never sell, rent or share your details for marketing.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-post mt-12">
      <h2 id="who">Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        This website is run by Carlos Leandro da Cunha Moreira, an individual based in Auckland, New Zealand ("I", "me").
        I am the agency responsible for your personal information under the New Zealand Privacy Act 2020.
        To contact me about privacy, use the <a href="/contact/?topic=privacy">contact form</a> and choose
        "A privacy request about my data".
      </p>

      <h2 id="what">What I collect and why</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Information</th><th>Why</th><th>Kept for</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Name, email, topic and message you send through the contact form, plus the date you agreed to this notice and which version you agreed to</td>
            <td>To read and reply to your message</td>
            <td>{RETENTION_MESSAGES}, then deleted automatically</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>A one-way, salted hash of your IP address (not the address itself)</td>
            <td>To limit how many messages one connection can send, so the form isn't abused</td>
            <td>{RETENTION_RATE_LIMIT}</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Technical request data (IP address, browser user agent) processed by the hosting and security providers listed below</td>
            <td>To deliver the pages and protect the site from attacks and abusive bots</td>
            <td>Under each provider's own retention policy</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        Your theme choice (light or dark) is saved in your own browser's local storage. It never leaves your device and
        I can't see it. I don't use cookies.
      </p>
      <p>
        I collect information directly from you (Privacy Act, IPP 2) and only what I need to reply (IPP 1). Filling in
        the form is voluntary; if you leave out your name, email or message, I simply can't reply. The form is not
        intended for children; please don't use it if you are under 16.
      </p>

      <h2 id="who-else">Who else processes it</h2>
      <p>I use a small number of service providers. Each holds or processes information on my behalf, on my instructions and only for the purposes above.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Supabase</strong> stores contact-form messages, in a database hosted in {DATABASE_REGION}.</li>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> provides DNS, security and the Turnstile spam check on the contact form. Turnstile loads only after you start filling in the form, and it checks signals from your browser to tell people from bots without tracking cookies.</li>
        <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong> hosts the website files and, like any web server, processes your IP address to deliver them.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        "Share on LinkedIn" buttons are plain links. LinkedIn receives nothing from this site unless you click one.
      </p>

      <h2 id="overseas">Sending information overseas</h2>
      <p>
        These providers store or process information outside New Zealand, including in Australia, the United States and
        other countries where they operate. They hold the information as my agents, so it stays my responsibility under
        the Privacy Act (section 11), and I rely on their contractual commitments (data processing agreements) to
        protect it in a way that provides safeguards comparable to the Privacy Act (IPP 12).
      </p>

      <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask me to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>confirm whether I hold information about you and give you a copy (Privacy Act IPP 6);</li>
        <li>correct it, or, if I don't agree it needs correcting, attach a statement of the correction you asked for (IPP 7).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The Privacy Act doesn't give a right to deletion, but I'll also delete your message on request, and I delete
        messages automatically after {RETENTION_MESSAGES} (IPP 9).
      </p>
      <p>
        I'll respond within 20 working days (the Privacy Act limit). There is no charge.
        I may need to confirm it's really you before handing over information.
      </p>

      <h2 id="security">How I protect it</h2>
      <p>
        To keep information safe (IPP 5), the public website is a set of static files: visitors' browsers never connect
        to the database. The database refuses all access from the public internet except through a single, validated
        contact endpoint, which checks the spam token, limits how often it can be used and rejects malformed input.
        Connections are encrypted (HTTPS), access to the data is limited to me, and secrets are kept out of the code.
      </p>
      <p>
        If a privacy breach ever happens that is likely to cause serious harm, I will notify the Office of the Privacy
        Commissioner and the people affected as soon as practicable, as Part 6 of the Privacy Act requires.
      </p>

      <h2 id="complaints">Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        Please contact me first so I can put things right. If you're not satisfied, you can complain to
        the <a href="https://www.privacy.org.nz/your-rights/making-a-complaint/">Office of the Privacy Commissioner</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="content-use">Use of this site's content</h2>
      <p>
        The writing, images and code samples on this site are my own work. I reserve the rights to text and data mining
        of this content, including for training artificial intelligence systems.
        Quoting with attribution and a link is welcome.
      </p>

      <h2 id="changes">Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>
        If I change how I handle personal information, I'll update this page and its version number. Messages are always
        stored with the version you agreed to.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
